{
  "_why": "The optimizer's role vocabulary (spec 15, rulings 2026-08-11). A role names 2-3 PRIMARY power-metric axes to push as hard as the rules allow, floors for the rest, and the spine choices that serve them: stat priority, weapon policy, enhancement split, gear ladders, feat spine, dips. The class_roles map picks each class's candidate roles; the generator samples one per character. Tune the JSON, not the engine (the build_archetypes.json precedent). Every vocabulary here is gated by scripts/gates/validate_power_roles.py against the code's own constants in utils/class_func/power_role.py -- a misspelled axis, token, feat or class name fails the build instead of contributing nothing forever.",
  "_floors_note": "Floors are PROVISIONAL until the optimized A/B distribution exists (ruling 9: measure first, then fix). They are ratio-vs-CR-benchmark bounds asserted by the gate, never the optimizer's stopping rule. dpr is deliberately never floored -- a controller wizard's weapon damage is allowed to be terrible. Race stays random under optimization, so floors must absorb race variance. Tuned once already, by the gate's own first run (2026-08-11): low-level will/ref floors were breaking on honest 4d6 variance.",
  "_no_blaster_note": "A burst-caster ROLE was cut from v1 by its own gate run: the only class it fit (kineticist) has metric-blind blast damage, so the role starved the weapon budget and lost to its random twin. The burst_raw AXIS stays (alpha uses it); the role returns when the optimizer grows a blast lever to pull -- a kineticist blast rule, or destruction-sphere leaf scoring.",
  "_margins_note": "MEASURED then made ROBUST, per ruling 9 -- remeasured twice: after the ambient-feat fold, then after v2 (alpha burst min 1.34, striker dpr min 1.79), then after the v3 wall pass (wall ac_combat min 1.44 / med 1.68; its hp tail dipped to 1.03 once the wildshape druid joined the role) (Power Attack alone moved the optimized striker median from 1.50 to 2.06). Source: a 112-generation optimized sweep (each role's mapped classes x L5/10/15/20, wealth-by-level, 4d6), bars set under the sweep MINIMUM (not p25 -- 16 samples underestimate the cross-seed tail, proven twice). Ratchet by re-running the sweep in tests/test_optimized_builds.py's header at higher n. caster_tier carries no margin (chassis, level-scaled, not a lever); the sniper dpr bar is honestly low -- ranged damage carries no ability modifier in metric or model, the recorded next lever for that role.",
